id: poison-vial
name: Poison Vial
kind: gear
craftDC: Expert
# "When you create this Basic Item, it has 1d6 Poison Drops." Rolled when it is given, and
# editable on the Item.
chargesDice: 1d6
chargesLabel: Poison Drops
source: Core Rule
description: >
  1d6 Poison Drops. An Action and a Drop poison a Weapon until the Combat Encounter ends.
text: >
  Poison Vial: A vial containing a deadly poison to use against your enemies.
  –Craft DC: Expert
  –Effects: When you create this Basic Item, it has 1d6 Poison Drops. You may spend 1 Action
  and 1 Poison Drop to Poison a Weapon. A Poisoned Weapon inflicts the Poisoned Combat
  Condition to a Character if you knock them through a Health Threshold with an Attacking
  Maneuver using that Weapon.

  A Weapon stops being Poisoned at the end of the Combat Encounter.

---

# --- What is built -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Poison Drops: 1d6, rolled when the character is given the Vial, shown on its row and
# editable on the Item.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Everything the Drops are for is about a Weapon, and there are no Weapons in this system yet -
# they arrive with Equipment. When they do: an Action and a Drop mark one of the character's
# Weapons Poisoned until the Combat Encounter ends, and an Attacking Maneuver made with it that
# knocks someone through a Health Threshold gives them Poisoned - the same moment Elemental
# (Fire)'s Broken is handed out.
